@osuki-dev/ui 2.0.0: ToastViewport returns null as soon as the toast array is
empty, while the last ToastCard is still running its 140 ms exiting animation.
Reanimated then finishes the exit on a child whose parent Fabric has already
deleted, which on Android is a fatal "Unable to find parentView for tag" in
SurfaceMountingManager.removeViewAt (seen on a physical phone, 2026-10-31 and
2026-11-01). Keep the absolutely positioned, box-none viewport mounted while
empty; it paints nothing and takes no touches.

Remove when upstream @osuki-dev/ui keeps the viewport mounted while empty (or
drops the card's exiting animation).

